During verification, /actuator/conditions on a debug-exposed instance of
loan-application-service showed OtlpTracingConfigurations.ConnectionDetails
unmatched against the brief-literal property 'management.otlp.tracing.endpoint'
(the Spring Boot 3.x property name):

  OtlpTracingConfigurations.ConnectionDetails#otlpTracingConnectionDetails
   - OnPropertyCondition @ConditionalOnProperty (management.opentelemetry.tracing.export.otlp.endpoint)
     did not find property (management.opentelemetry.tracing.export.otlp.endpoint)

This meant NO SpanExporter/OtlpHttpSpanExporter bean was ever created and the
app made ZERO network attempts to the OTLP endpoint (confirmed via lsof - no
socket to :4317/:4318, not even a failed one) despite Tracer/Propagator beans
existing and Maestro's TracingEngineObserver correctly creating real spans
(non-zero W3C trace/span IDs observed in MDC-correlated log lines).

application.yml was corrected to the Spring Boot 4.0.5 property path
(management.opentelemetry.tracing.export.otlp.endpoint) in all three services.
After the fix, /actuator/beans showed a genuine 'otlpHttpSpanExporter' bean,
and a temporary local HTTP listener on 127.0.0.1:4318/[::1]:4318 (standing in
for a real OTLP collector, since Jaeger is deliberately not part of this
task's verification per the brief) received real OTLP/HTTP protobuf POSTs
to /v1/traces while a loan was driven through loan-application-service:

RECEIVED POST /v1/traces len=1933 from=('::1', 56416, 0, 0)
RECEIVED POST /v1/traces len=561 from=('::1', 56417, 0, 0)
RECEIVED POST /v1/traces len=561 from=('::1', 56424, 0, 0)
RECEIVED POST /v1/traces len=561 from=('::1', 56426, 0, 0)

(3-4 POSTs of realistic protobuf-encoded batch sizes, confirming spans for
the run/activity segments were genuinely exported over OTLP/HTTP - not just
a bean existing inertly.)
